WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.700
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.702
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.836
We hope you're
doing well tonight

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:04.703
and now, we're going
to get to the news.

00:00:04.703 --> 00:00:05.605
In an interview

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.006
with CNN last night,

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:10.676
White House Press Secretary
Karine Jean-Pierre was asked

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:13.213
if President Biden's age
or stamina

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.914
will be a challenge
in his reelection bid.

00:00:15.914 --> 00:00:17.449
Said Jean-Pierre, "No,

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:18.685
everything else will."

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.520
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.889
President Biden criticized
large corporations

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.225
for keeping prices high
to boost profits,

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.792
in a speech last week, and said,

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:30.029
"Exxon made more money than God
last year."

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.631
Worse, they made it by selling
a natural resource,

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:35.201
so that's technically
God's money.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.970
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.471
During her opening statement

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.373
at yesterday's hearing
on the Capitol attack,

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.176
Republican Representative
Liz Cheney said that

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:46.446
an "apparently inebriated
Rudy Giuliani

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.647
told former President Trump

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:50.383
to falsely claim he won
on election night."

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.184
To be fair, his legal advice

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:53.986
doesn't get any better
when he's sober.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:55.821
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:57.023
"Are you drunk again?"

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.591
[ As Giuliani ]
Trust me, it's just as bad.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.526
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:03.263
During yesterday's congressional
hearing, it was revealed

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.831
that Donald Trump Jr.'s fiancée,
Kimberly Guilfoyle,

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:09.969
was paid $60,000 to speak at the
rally before the Capitol attack.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.238
Well, technically,
$20,000 to speak

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.208
and then $40,000 to please stop.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.676
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.010
When asked if he will support

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.413
the bipartisan
gun legislation framework,

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.683
Republican Senator Mike Braun
said he was open to it,

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.452
but added he was,
"interested to see

00:01:26.452 --> 00:01:27.887
where the NRA is on it,"

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:31.124
which is a little like saying
you're open to eating healthier,

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:34.961
but are interested to see
how Oreos feel about it, first.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.396
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.931
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
over the weekend appeared

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:41.700
on an episode of
"RuPaul's Drag Race All Stars."

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:45.270
Either that, or she didn't,
and that person should win.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.141
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.543
I mean --

00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:54.314
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.783
Mick Jagger announced yesterday

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.852
he tested positive
for the coronavirus

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:02.121
and Keith Richards announced
that's the only thing

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:03.822
he's tested negative for.

00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:06.893
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:10.730
Beyoncé recently deleted
her profile pictures

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.231
on all social media platforms.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.735
I just hope I can remember
what Beyoncé looks like.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.269
[ Subdued laughter ]

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:19.605
Former President Trump
turned 76 today,

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:22.942
so now, he's really asking
everyone to stop the count.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.945
[ Laughter and groans ]

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.280
That's right, today was
former President Donald Trump's

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.149
76th birthday.
Pretty impressive --

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:33.252
76, and he can still get
an insurrection.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:36.188
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:39.192
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.262
That man was our president!

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:45.965
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.603
And, finally, rapper Snoop Dogg
recently tweeted

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:53.138
that the full-time blunt roller
he hired

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:56.642
now makes up to $50,000 a year,

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.745
which has to be the smallest
salary she's ever made.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:02.114
[ Laughter and ohs ]

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.716
I bet they're
beautifully rolled.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.819
[ Laughter ]
I bet they're beautifully,
artisanally rolled.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.887
That was a monologue, everybody.

